00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:13.210
Imagine you added a Canadian bank stock to your TFSA last quarter expecting steady income.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:20.290
The dividend arrived, yet the after-tax yield looked different once compared to a US name in the same account.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:24.830
Eligible Canadian dividends qualify for the dividend tax credit.

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:30.630
That credit can reduce the effective tax rate to near zero for investors in lower brackets.

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:37.290
The Canadian dividend aristocrats lists supplies names with 22-5 plus years of increases.

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:46.170
Sustainability hinges on payout ratios below 60% of free cash flow and coverage ratios above 1.5 times.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:51.970
Dividend growth strategies have outperformed high yield approaches over full market cycles.

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:57.310
They compound at lower initial yields while avoiding payout cuts during recessions.

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:07.090
DRIP programs at the big banks and pipelines let you reinvest automatically inside the TFSA without triggering contribution room issues.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:14.710
The bank pipeline telecom oligopoly gives these names pricing power that supports payouts through commodity cycles.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:24.750
Stuffing at TFSA with a diversified basket of these names remains popular because the tax credit and contribution room growth compound together.

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:29.310
The biggest misconception is assuming any high yield is sustainable.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:33.270
Always cross-check free cash flow coverage before adding size.

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:40.550
Investors often overlook that the gross up and tax credit mechanism applies only to eligible Canadian dividends.

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:47.190
It does not apply to foreign dividends or distributions from US companies held inside the same account.

00:10:47.550 --> 00:11:01.590
This distinction matters when constructing a TFSA because a 4% yield from a Canadian bank can deliver more after tax cash than a 5% yield from a US utility once foreign withholding tax is factored in.

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:07.990
Free cash flow coverage above 1.5 times provides a buffer during economic slowdowns.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:13.070
Companies can maintain or grow dividends even when earnings dip temporarily.

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:19.050
The big 5 banks and major pipelines have demonstrated this resilience across multiple cycles.

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:25.630
Automatic DRIP enrollment inside at TFSA also avoids any cash drag.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:30.310
It keeps the full contribution room available for new deposits each year.

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:36.590
The strategies edge comes from combining the tax credit with the TFSA's tax-free growth.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:46.370
That edge holds only when the underlying holdings maintain sustainable payout ratios supported by actual cash generation rather than debt-funded distributions.

